<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Umkhonto we Sizwe</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1961">1961</a>–<a href="/years/1993">1993</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as MK</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Umkhonto we Sizwe (&quot;Spear of the Nation&quot;), or MK, was the armed wing of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/african-national-congress">African National Congress</a>, founded in December 1961 with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-african-communist-party">South African Communist Party</a> after the banning of the ANC. Led at first by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nelson-mandela">Nelson Mandela</a>, it began with sabotage and later waged a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guerrilla-warfare">guerrilla</a> campaign from bases in neighbouring countries. It suspended armed struggle in 1990 and joined the national army in 1994.</p></div>
